From e5fab02325d13fb8b7796c479916cc29a0ef6f4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bitbonsai <44185+bitbonsai@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:49:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Keep native sidebar contents fixed during slide

Optional 0010 candidate. Apply after 0009-rust-workspace-sidebar.patch
from project commit 0de7a7f78a807683a0ecf686893a79d614340e7e.
Baseline: external Chromium 3e117efa80cec1c4e1e6fbfdf44edeb087a279a5
with the current native parity stack and independent endpoint rounding.
Full index hashes identify each exact input file.

Keep header, legacy body and optional workspace body at the existing
expanded target width. Translate logical bounds together inside the
region clip; leave animation, reversal and reduced-motion ownership with
BrowserAnimationController. Preserve expanded group, grid and New Tab
presentation. Reserve the existing trailing gutter in TabStripViewLayout
instead of subtracting another inset inside each pin or split.

Includes a native bounds regression for the parent to run. Scratch
source-derived geometry assertions and real-header syntax checks passed;
native recordings, reduced motion, focus, caption controls, popup anchors
and fullscreen/RTL runtime acceptance remain unverified.
